## Why This Is Asked
This assesses real-world decision making for cost-aware routing, tenant isolation, and auditable ops in a regulated cloud environment.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant policy engine for cost and latency governance
- Dynamic routing to multiple Azure OpenAI deployments
- Grounding decisions with Cognitive Search KBs and versioned storage
- Auditable telemetry to Data Lake and RBAC with Azure AD

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: simple routing decision based on tenant budget and SLA
function selectDeployment(tenant, metrics){
  if (metrics.latencyMs <= tenant.sla && tenant.budget >= 0.6) return 'gpt-4o';
  if (metrics.tokens < 1000 && tenant.budget < 0.6) return 'gpt-3.5-turbo';
  return 'private-finetuned';
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test budget enforcement at scale across tenants?
- What edge cases require fallback routing and how would you implement it?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a scalable, compliant multi-tenant NLP assistant with data isolation and governance across Azure services.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented generation with per-tenant Cognitive Search KB
- Per-tenant RBAC using Azure AD
- PII redaction via Text Analytics
- Prompt ownership governed by a policy registry
- Canary-based prompt rollouts and end-to-end testing with synthetic tenants

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: tenant-scoped lookup and prompt assembly
async function respond(tenantId, userQuery){
  const kb = await kbClient.getTenantKB(tenantId);
  const prompt = buildPrompt(tenantId, userQuery, kb);
  const redacted = await piiRedactor.redact(userQuery);
  const res = await openai.complete({prompt});
  await logMetrics(tenantId, res);
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement per-tenant data masking across Data Lake and tracing?
- How would you audit and rollback prompt changes in production?

## Why This Is Asked
